axes.tools:
The MCP surface has multiple official pages: Cosmos Experts connect MCP servers (MCP Registry), CLI/IDE-side MCP configuration,
Context Engine MCP (plugging the context engine into any agent via MCP), MCP context hookup for Code Review;
the official side also ships a Docs MCP server (Streamable HTTP) so external agents can query Augment docs.

axes.context:
The signature is the Code Context Engine: the official stance is a world-class context engine with structured cross-codebase understanding;
it is exported as MCP for other agents to use (Context Engine MCP page).
Wisdom-class context (PR history, business requirements) is expanded on the Software Factory loop pages.

axes.permissions:
Enterprise positioning (the enterprise-grade stance runs through the official docs): Trust Center and Status Page entries sit in the navigation;
the Analytics API uses scoped OAuth tokens or service-account bearer tokens, with write permissions requested on demand (per the official llms.txt).
The individual-side permission model was not verified item by item.
